    "public_api_change": "ADDITIVE",
    "schema_diff_summary": "document.rs has one test module named tests. Add the new test function at the end of that module, before its closing brace. Do not write a second mod tests. Add is_error on impl MarkKind. Keep it public, the same way is_execution is public. Do not add a dead_code attribute. The body is matches!(self, Self::Error). Do not write if self == Self::Error { true } else { false }.  Do not write two if arms that return the same value. Combine them with ||. That is clippy::if_same_then_else. Do not touch is_diagnostic, is_bookmark, or is_execution. The existing test a_warning_kind_is_a_diagnostic stays green. Do not rewrite its assertions. The test an_error_kind_is_an_error checks MarkKind::Error is true. MarkKind::Warning is false. MarkKind::Bookmark is false. MarkKind::Execution is false. Branch from the current tip of main. base_sha records that tip at planning time. If main has moved, use the new tip. Keep the change under about 60 lines. Stay inside this one behavior. Run the full test module named in the commands, not only the new test."
  },
